1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:04,629
[BEA] <i>Ma, why are there only three plates?</i>

2
00:00:04,713 --> 00:00:08,049
<i>Is Papa not coming home?</i>
<i>Isn't he joining us?</i>

3
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:09,884
[MARIELA]
<i>You really take after your father.</i>

4
00:00:09,968 --> 00:00:11,845
<i>You're both useless!</i>

5
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:16,474
<i>Are you going to take his side? Huh?</i>

6
00:00:16,558 --> 00:00:20,061
<i>Then get out of here and go with him!</i>

7
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:23,440
<i>You deserve each other anyway!</i>

8
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:30,864
- [MARIELA SCREAMING]
- [PLATES SHATTERING]

9
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:37,203
<i>Ma.</i>

10
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:38,872
<i>Don't tell them</i>

11
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:41,916
<i>that you know</i>
<i>they're Papa's second family.</i>

12
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:44,586
<i>Why not?</i>

13
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:46,713
[BEA] <i>That's a strong motive.</i>

14
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:50,800
<i>It'll just prove that you're going after</i>
<i>Papa's illegitimate child.</i>

15
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:53,511
<i>We'll get into more trouble.</i>

16
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:55,889
[ENRICO] <i>I don't know if Billy will ever</i>
<i>be able to forgive me</i>

17
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:57,348
<i>for what I'm about to tell her.</i>

18
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:59,684
<i>But she needs to know the truth.</i>

19
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:03,480
<i>You know, I've always wondered,</i>

20
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:07,233
<i>"What if you'd been there</i>
<i>the night Oliver was born?"</i>

21
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:09,861
<i>"Would Mama still be alive?"</i>

22
00:01:13,364 --> 00:01:15,075
<i>Because I knew that if you were there,</i>

23
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:16,826
<i>you wouldn't abandon us.</i>

24
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:23,083
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

25
00:01:26,377 --> 00:01:29,214
[SOBBING]

26
00:01:29,297 --> 00:01:31,007
<i>I hope you can all forgive me.</i>

27
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:38,640
<i>Billy, are you sure you're ready?</i>

28
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:41,726
<i>We don't really have a choice.</i>

29
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:45,605
<i>LoveList can't afford to slow down now.</i>

30
00:01:45,688 --> 00:01:48,066
<i>Jumping in on the budget discussion,</i>

31
00:01:48,149 --> 00:01:50,485
<i>I'll also present the projected cost</i>

32
00:01:50,568 --> 00:01:53,696
<i>for our new security upgrades.</i>

33
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,116
<i>How bad are the numbers?</i>

34
00:01:56,199 --> 00:01:58,201
<i>They are pretty high, chief.</i>

35
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:02,038
<i>Then we really don't have a choice.</i>

36
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:04,999
<i>We need to close this deal</i>
<i>with Claire Fabrizio.</i>

37
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:06,126
<i>Okay?</i>

38
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:08,336
- [PHONE CHIMES]
- [ROWENA] <i>Ralph! Son.</i>

39
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:11,339
[CHUCKLES] <i>My son.</i>

40
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,510
<i>Say hi to your aunties.</i>

41
00:02:15,593 --> 00:02:17,595
<i>- Ah…</i>
<i>- My son, Ralph.</i>

42
00:02:17,679 --> 00:02:18,721
<i>Hello.</i>

43
00:02:20,014 --> 00:02:21,349
<i>I heard the news.</i>

44
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:24,769
<i>The drama of that company, it never ends.</i>

45
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:27,814
<i>Ma, please. Come on.</i>

46
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:32,152
<i>I told you, it's a mess there.</i>

47
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:35,864
<i>That company is bound to fail</i>
<i>sooner or later.</i>

48
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:37,699
<i>Get out while you still can.</i>

49
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:44,038
<i>Okay.</i>

50
00:02:45,915 --> 00:02:48,126
<i>You know I just want</i>
<i>what's best for you, son.</i>

51
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:50,461
<i>What's best for me?</i>

52
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:53,298
<i>What's best for me</i>

53
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:56,801
<i>is for you to stop controlling</i>
<i>all my decisions.</i>

54
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:00,013
<i>Wow.</i>

55
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:03,016
<i>You don't get it, do you?</i>

56
00:03:04,475 --> 00:03:06,644
<i>I'm doing all this for your sake.</i>

57
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:09,856
<i>For your future.</i>

58
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:18,615
Ma.

59
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:21,075
I spoke with the lawyer.

60
00:03:21,576 --> 00:03:25,038
She said it's possible
you'll be moved to a hospital.

61
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:27,665
Isn't that great, Ma?

62
00:03:28,249 --> 00:03:30,460
You won't rot here anymore.

63
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:31,920
You can get out.

64
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:33,755
Which hospital?

65
00:03:33,838 --> 00:03:37,425
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

66
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:38,968
The…

67
00:03:41,721 --> 00:03:42,639
ward.

68
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:45,433
- She's crazy. She's going to a psych ward.
- [MARIELA] Wait, the psych ward?

69
00:03:45,516 --> 00:03:47,227
- What am I, crazy?
- [LAUGHS] She admitted it.

70
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:49,187
You want to be away from me, right?

71
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:51,314
- [WOMAN] It came from her.
- Ma, no. You're not crazy.

72
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:56,152
Ma, just think about it.
You'll be better off there.

73
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:58,196
You'll be taken care of.

74
00:03:58,279 --> 00:04:00,156
Turns out she really is crazy.

75
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,158
- [WOMEN CACKLING]
- She belongs there.

76
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:03,910
- Ma. Hey, Ma!
- Hey!

77
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:05,536
- Let go of me! Ouch!
- Stop it, Ma!

78
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,372
- [WOMAN] Stay out of this!
- [BEA] What the hell?!

79
00:04:07,455 --> 00:04:09,540
- Stop it!
- Ma! Ma!

80
00:04:11,292 --> 00:04:13,086
- [GRUNTS SOFTLY]
- Ma!

81
00:04:14,295 --> 00:04:17,465
- Miss! Miss, help! Help!
- [WOMAN] Hey! Hey! Hey!

82
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:19,550
- Hey! What's going on there?!
- Hey! Here she comes!

83
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:21,552
[WOMAN] They started it! They're psychos!

84
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:23,471
Stop it! Quiet down!

85
00:04:23,554 --> 00:04:26,766
My mother needs a doctor!
Miss, call a doctor!

86
00:04:26,849 --> 00:04:28,810
My mother needs one now!

87
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:35,608
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

88
00:05:16,065 --> 00:05:17,066
Boss.

89
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:18,901
[OVERLAPPING, INDISTINCT CHATTER]

90
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:22,613
- Is this tequila?
- Uh, yes.

91
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:26,826
[YANI] We're starting early.
Speaking of which, let's do a shot.

92
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:29,912
[INDISTINCT CHATTER CONTINUES]

93
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:32,707
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]
- [FRIENDS GUSHING]

94
00:05:32,790 --> 00:05:36,169
[RALPH] Okay. Perfect, perfect.
Just right, just right.

95
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:38,671
Okay, cheers

96
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:40,923
to our second anniversary, babe.

97
00:05:41,632 --> 00:05:42,508
- Come on.
- Cheers.

98
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:43,718
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

99
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:44,927
Happy second anniversary!

100
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:46,345
- Cheers, everyone!
- Cheers, guys!

101
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:48,222
- Oh, yes.
- Cheers!

102
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:50,183
Mm-hmm.

103
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,602
Ah!

104
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:53,811
[RALPH] There you go.

105
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:55,521
- [YANI] Whoo!
- [RALPH] That's so good. Mmm!

106
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:56,981
[YANI] Oh!

107
00:05:57,065 --> 00:05:58,441
- [RALPH] Is it okay?
- [YANI] Uh-huh!

108
00:05:58,524 --> 00:06:00,735
- [GLASSES CLINKING]
- [TONI] You want more?

109
00:06:00,818 --> 00:06:02,779
What? Still working?

110
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:05,114
I have to.

111
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:06,657
Thanks for the treat!

112
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:08,493
[YANI] Oh, right.

113
00:06:08,576 --> 00:06:10,745
Toni said it was just going to be
you two celebrating.

114
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:11,662
What happened?

115
00:06:13,539 --> 00:06:14,582
Uh, well…

116
00:06:14,665 --> 00:06:16,626
We wanted to celebrate with you guys.

117
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:20,088
I mean, come on, it's more fun
to celebrate with friends, right?

118
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:21,464
- Right.
- Yeah?

119
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:22,799
- [TONI] Is that so?
- [YANI] Okay.

120
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:25,384
Well then, cheers to the couple!

121
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:26,552
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

122
00:06:26,636 --> 00:06:27,762
- Cheers, guys.
- Okay.

123
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:28,888
- Cheers!
- Cheers, guys!

124
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:30,890
- To justice!
- Yes!

125
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:32,558
- To justice.
- [CHUCKLES]

126
00:06:33,142 --> 00:06:36,145
Good thing those menaces are
behind bars now, chief.

127
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:37,480
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

128
00:06:37,563 --> 00:06:38,523
[BLAIRE] Huh?

129
00:06:40,858 --> 00:06:41,734
Billy.

130
00:06:44,904 --> 00:06:46,697
- Yes?
- Guys.

131
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:49,200
This is about Charm and Ralph.

132
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:51,327
Let's stop stressing out.

133
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:52,370
Right?

134
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:54,330
Here. Dude.

135
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:58,751
- [YANI] This one's good.
- [CLINKS]

136
00:06:58,835 --> 00:06:59,877
[TONI] Wait, it is.

137
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:01,629
- [YANI] So good!
- [BLAIRE] I think it's shrimp.

138
00:07:01,712 --> 00:07:04,090
- This one too!
- [BLAIRE] It's so fresh!

139
00:07:04,173 --> 00:07:05,967
It's just a minor cut.

140
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:07,260
Huh? A minor cut?

141
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:11,222
Doc, my mother hit her head pretty hard.
You're saying it's just a minor cut?

142
00:07:11,305 --> 00:07:13,349
She should be transferred to a hospital!

143
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,268
Nurse, call on the guards.

144
00:07:15,351 --> 00:07:17,145
They may be taken back to their cells.

145
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:19,021
Ah-- Doc!

146
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:22,275
[SIGHS] She should be at the hospital.

147
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:24,902
[SIGHS]

148
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:25,903
Let's go, Ma.

149
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:27,905
- [GRUNTS AGGRESSIVELY]
- Rest up--

150
00:07:27,989 --> 00:07:30,408
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

151
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:31,576
What's wrong?

152
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:35,413
You want me to get sent
to the mental hospital.

153
00:07:35,496 --> 00:07:37,415
You want to get rid of me!

154
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:39,167
Ma, that's not it!

155
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:42,253
I don't want to see you
in such a sorry state.

156
00:07:42,336 --> 00:07:44,672
I can't stand seeing you suffer.

157
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:48,634
That's why you should be transferred
to a hospital. A general hospital.

158
00:07:48,718 --> 00:07:52,096
If I get transferred to a hospital,
you won't be there.

159
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:57,059
That's why I don't want to!
I don't want to!

160
00:07:57,143 --> 00:07:59,854
- [SHUSHING] Ma, calm down.
- I don't want to!

161
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:02,190
- Okay, okay.
- I don't want to go there!

162
00:08:02,273 --> 00:08:04,025
That's enough, Ma.

163
00:08:04,108 --> 00:08:07,111
- Don't force me!
- Okay, I won't.

164
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:13,409
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

165
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:19,916
Bro, I'll be right back.

166
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:28,549
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

167
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:36,349
VISTING AREA RULES

168
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:50,071
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

169
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,198
What do you want?

170
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:55,159
Let me join your group.

171
00:08:56,661 --> 00:08:57,912
I can help.

172
00:08:57,995 --> 00:08:59,288
Promise.

173
00:09:00,122 --> 00:09:02,083
What help are you talking about?

174
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:08,422
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

175
00:09:08,506 --> 00:09:10,049
I know about your plan.

176
00:09:11,634 --> 00:09:14,220
- On Family Day, right?
- [SUSPENSEFUL STING]

177
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:15,930
Keep your mouth shut.

178
00:09:17,014 --> 00:09:18,808
Please, hear me out.

179
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:21,435
[CALOY] Listen.

180
00:09:23,104 --> 00:09:24,355
Once you get out of here,

181
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:27,149
what'll you do?

182
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:28,693
Go into hiding for the rest of your life?

183
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:31,487
How is that any different
from being imprisoned?

184
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,741
I can help you.

185
00:09:38,077 --> 00:09:39,370
I know someone.

186
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:41,914
He can give us new names

187
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:44,041
and a new life.

188
00:09:45,876 --> 00:09:48,129
We can live as a different person

189
00:09:48,212 --> 00:09:49,755
without anyone going after us.

190
00:09:52,133 --> 00:09:53,259
[EXHALES]

191
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:54,594
But before that,

192
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:57,888
of course you need to let me in your group

193
00:09:57,972 --> 00:10:00,224
and help me get out of here too.

194
00:10:02,768 --> 00:10:04,228
So I can finally be with her.

195
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:11,277
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

196
00:10:18,117 --> 00:10:20,786
[ROCK MUSIC PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

197
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,788
Um, Billy?

198
00:10:24,165 --> 00:10:28,127
Some of your stuff is still in my unit.

199
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:29,754
I'll just send it to you.

200
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:33,924
You know you can still stay there, right?

201
00:10:34,008 --> 00:10:36,010
You just want to leave
as soon as possible.

202
00:10:36,093 --> 00:10:38,262
No, it's all good. Thank you, Charm.

203
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:42,391
There's just too many of us.

204
00:10:42,475 --> 00:10:44,727
My father is staying with us now too.

205
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:46,771
Thank you.

206
00:10:49,732 --> 00:10:50,941
You're on good terms now?

207
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:58,532
He saved Oliver and Aunt Pres, so…

208
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:01,243
I owe him that.

209
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:04,664
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

210
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:06,957
You won't regret your decision, Billy.

211
00:11:08,125 --> 00:11:10,002
And I'm happy for you.

212
00:11:10,961 --> 00:11:12,380
[CHARM] Because

213
00:11:13,422 --> 00:11:15,883
you won't go through what I experienced.

214
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:20,638
Babe?

215
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:24,683
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

216
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:25,976
[SIGHS]

217
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:29,438
You know that

218
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:32,733
my mother is a single parent, right?

219
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:39,865
And I used to always make her feel that

220
00:11:40,449 --> 00:11:43,411
what she was doing for me wasn't enough.

221
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:46,122
Because of that,

222
00:11:47,623 --> 00:11:49,917
she felt she had to work abroad.

223
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,710
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:11:52,336 --> 00:11:53,546
But…

225
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:55,631
[INHALES SHARPLY]

226
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:59,051
…she had only been abroad for a few years…

227
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:03,764
when she got into an accident.

228
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,103
She died.

229
00:12:09,186 --> 00:12:11,439
[CHARM BREATHES DEEPLY]

230
00:12:11,522 --> 00:12:13,357
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

231
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:16,068
I blame it on myself because…

232
00:12:19,405 --> 00:12:21,907
she wouldn't have left
if it weren't for me.

233
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:25,494
But do you know what hurts more than that?

234
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:32,334
[BREATHES SHAKILY]

235
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:34,545
She died while we were
still not on good terms.

236
00:12:34,628 --> 00:12:40,426
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

237
00:12:40,509 --> 00:12:43,220
I wasn't able to ask for her forgiveness.

238
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:49,059
[CHARM SNIFFLES]

239
00:12:49,143 --> 00:12:50,352
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

240
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:54,523
[CHARM] Before,

241
00:12:55,399 --> 00:12:57,318
I wanted you to stand your ground.

242
00:12:57,401 --> 00:12:59,028
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

243
00:12:59,111 --> 00:13:01,363
I always told you that I hoped…

244
00:13:04,617 --> 00:13:06,702
you'd learn how to fight.

245
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:13,876
But now that it has come to this…

246
00:13:13,959 --> 00:13:17,046
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:13:17,129 --> 00:13:20,549
I'm reminded of how I didn't
obey my mother back then.

